# Tile packs — ~10 GB, rebuilt by tools/download-tiles.ts + pack-pmtiles.ts.
# Never commit these; the Pi gets them out of band, not through git.
#
# `data/`, not `static/`: under static/ Vite copies and brotli-compresses all
# ~56k of them into build/ on every build, and serves them outside the
# /api/tiles guard. Moved 2026-09-03.
data/tiles/

# The persisted wall snapshot — RUNTIME state, not source.
#
# `pushWall` writes this on every operator push and `readWall` loads it at boot,
# so it is per-device state that happens to live under data/. Committing one
# would ship whatever place, weather and display mode the last developer pushed
# as every device's boot state.
#
# It also outranks the URL, which is what makes a stray copy expensive to
# diagnose: a wall snapshot applies over `readSettings`, so a leftover
# `displayMode: 'flight'` silently beat `?mode=screensaver` and the smoke test
# reported "no media element mounted — MediaStage fell through to an empty
# state". The component was fine; the state underneath it was not.
data/wall.json
# Uploaded songs and clips. Content, not source — and a Pi's copy is its own.
data/media/

# Python bytecode — a survey script imported tools/*.py and this got swept in.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

